cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AgentCodec: A Communication-Theoretic Framework for LLM Agents"
message: >-
  If you use AgentCodec in academic work, please cite this software
  and the accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hamed
    family-names: Omidvar
    affiliation: INTELLERCE LLC
    email: research@intellerce.com
  - given-names: Vahideh
    family-names: Akhlaghi
    affiliation: INTELLERCE LLC
    email: research@intellerce.com
abstract: >-
  AgentCodec wraps every LLM call in a technique drawn from classical
  communication theory: HARQ for iterative refinement, diversity
  combining for ensembles, FEC for redundancy under budget pressure,
  ACM routing for adaptive coding/modulation. 29 dispatchable
  techniques in six families, plus 7 prior-method baselines. The
  SemKNN cost-aware router achieves up to ~56% cost reduction at
  matched quality, or ~7% quality improvement at matched cost, vs.
  prior baselines.
